\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The three objects for the specimen $21^8/5$ ($\Lambda =\{a\equiv b\ (4)\}$, $Q=[0,4]^2$; \emph  {exact computation}). (a)~The fibre $F(\Lambda ,Q)$: six points, the origin being excluded. (b)~The abstract complex $K_{\mathrm  {abs}}$: f-vector $(6,11,1)$, Betti numbers $(1,5,0)$; edges are drawn as arcs to stress that they are formal incidences, and the thick cycle bounds the single $2$-cell. (c)~The realised union $U$ of the closed cells with straight edges: it has two bounded complementary components (hatched), so $b_1(U)=2\ne  b_1(K_{\mathrm  {abs}})=5$. Edges of $K_{\mathrm  {abs}}$ cross inside the square, so closed cells do not all meet in common faces and $K_{\mathrm  {emb}}$ is \emph  {not} defined for this specimen. The Betti numbers agree with those reported by the release; $b_1(U)$ was obtained here with a floating-point polygon routine on exact integer coordinates (\cref  {def:cell}, \cref  {prop:topology}).}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:objects}{{1}{6}{The three objects for the specimen $21^8/5$ ($\Lambda =\{a\equiv b\ (4)\}$, $Q=[0,4]^2$; \emph {exact computation}). (a)~The fibre $F(\Lambda ,Q)$: six points, the origin being excluded. (b)~The abstract complex $\Kabs $: f-vector $(6,11,1)$, Betti numbers $(1,5,0)$; edges are drawn as arcs to stress that they are formal incidences, and the thick cycle bounds the single $2$-cell. (c)~The realised union $U$ of the closed cells with straight edges: it has two bounded complementary components (hatched), so $b_1(U)=2\ne b_1(\Kabs )=5$. Edges of $\Kabs $ cross inside the square, so closed cells do not all meet in common faces and $\Kemb $ is \emph {not} defined for this specimen. The Betti numbers agree with those reported by the release; $b_1(U)$ was obtained here with a floating-point polygon routine on exact integer coordinates (\cref {def:cell}, \cref {prop:topology})}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:objects@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][5][]6}}
