\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The exact corner-cube witness (\cref  {thm:evensum}; scaled $\Lambda =E_3\subset \Lambda '=\mathbb  Z^3$, box $(1,1,2)$; \emph  {exact computation}). (a)~The $2$-cell $\Pi ((0,0,2);(0,1,-1),(1,0,-1))$ of $K_{\mathrm  {abs}}(E_3,Q)$ (a realised parallelogram), the five points of the fibre $F(E_3,Q)$ and the corner cube $O=[0,1)^3$ (dashed); the star is the witness $(\frac  23,\frac  23,\frac  23)\in O$. (b)~Orthogonal projection to $(x_1,x_3)$, complementing the perspective view. (c)~The section $x_3=\frac  23$: the section of the cell (blue segment from $(1,\frac  13)$ to $(\frac  13,1)$) has its interior in the open square $O$, while the target union $U(\mathbb  Z^3,Q)$ at this height consists only of the lines $x_1=1$, $x_2=1$ (teal, dashed), met by the segment only at its end points. Hence the witness is not in $U(\mathbb  Z^3,Q)$. All three panels show realised objects; none shows $K_{\mathrm  {emb}}$.}}{17}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:corner}{{6}{17}{The exact corner-cube witness (\cref {thm:evensum}; scaled $\Lambda =E_3\subset \Lambda '=\Z ^3$, box $(1,1,2)$; \emph {exact computation}). (a)~The $2$-cell $\Pil ((0,0,2);(0,1,-1),(1,0,-1))$ of $\Kabs (E_3,Q)$ (a realised parallelogram), the five points of the fibre $F(E_3,Q)$ and the corner cube $O=[0,1)^3$ (dashed); the star is the witness $(\frac 23,\frac 23,\frac 23)\in O$. (b)~Orthogonal projection to $(x_1,x_3)$, complementing the perspective view. (c)~The section $x_3=\frac 23$: the section of the cell (blue segment from $(1,\frac 13)$ to $(\frac 13,1)$) has its interior in the open square $O$, while the target union $U(\Z ^3,Q)$ at this height consists only of the lines $x_1=1$, $x_2=1$ (teal, dashed), met by the segment only at its end points. Hence the witness is not in $U(\Z ^3,Q)$. All three panels show realised objects; none shows $\Kemb $}{figure.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:corner@cref}{{[figure][6][]6}{[1][16][]17}}
