\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Abstract loss versus realised containment (\cref  {thm:E28} and \cref  {thm:laws}(L3); planar specimen $21^{8}/5\to 21^{8}/4$, $h=4$, $Q=[0,4]^2$; \emph  {exact computation}, each edge checked exactly at $41$ points). (a)~Two edges $e_1$ (from $(0,4)$ to $(4,4)$, generator $(4,0)$) and $e_2$ (from $(0,4)$ to $(1,1)$, generator $(1,-3)$) of $K_{\mathrm  {abs}}(\Lambda ,Q)$, $\Lambda =\{a\equiv b\ (4)\}$; neither generator is Graver for $\Lambda '=\{a\equiv b\ (2)\}$, so both edges are lost in $K_{\mathrm  {abs}}(\Lambda ',Q)$. (b)~In the target complex $e_1$ is the union of two $(2,0)$-edges and $e_2$ is a diagonal of the shaded $2$-cell $\Pi ((0,2);(0,2),(1,-1))$. (c)~The unions: $U(\Lambda ',Q)$ (teal) contains $U(\Lambda ,Q)$ (blue outline), and the lost edges (red, dotted) lie inside it. Distinct objects: lost in $K_{\mathrm  {abs}}(\Lambda ',Q)$, contained in $U(\Lambda ',Q)$.}}{18}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lost}{{7}{18}{Abstract loss versus realised containment (\cref {thm:E28} and \cref {thm:laws}(L3); planar specimen $21^{8}/5\to 21^{8}/4$, $h=4$, $Q=[0,4]^2$; \emph {exact computation}, each edge checked exactly at $41$ points). (a)~Two edges $e_1$ (from $(0,4)$ to $(4,4)$, generator $(4,0)$) and $e_2$ (from $(0,4)$ to $(1,1)$, generator $(1,-3)$) of $\Kabs (\Lambda ,Q)$, $\Lambda =\{a\equiv b\ (4)\}$; neither generator is Graver for $\Lambda '=\{a\equiv b\ (2)\}$, so both edges are lost in $\Kabs (\Lambda ',Q)$. (b)~In the target complex $e_1$ is the union of two $(2,0)$-edges and $e_2$ is a diagonal of the shaded $2$-cell $\Pil ((0,2);(0,2),(1,-1))$. (c)~The unions: $U(\Lambda ',Q)$ (teal) contains $U(\Lambda ,Q)$ (blue outline), and the lost edges (red, dotted) lie inside it. Distinct objects: lost in $\Kabs (\Lambda ',Q)$, contained in $U(\Lambda ',Q)$}{figure.7}{}}
\newlabel{fig:lost@cref}{{[figure][7][]7}{[1][17][]18}}
